105
00:19:43,360 --> 00:19:50,400
This is from the Keynes essay: "There was extreme method in his madness. All his unpublished works on esoteric and theological matters are marked by

106
00:19:50,400 --> 00:19:59,440
careful learning, accurate method, and extreme sobriety of statement. They are just as sane as the Principia if their whole matter and purpose were not magical.

107
00:19:59,440 --> 00:20:12,240
They were nearly all composed during the same 25 years of his mathematical studies." Clearly, there was some aesthetic that motivated people like Einstein to reject earlier ways of

108
00:20:12,240 --> 00:20:24,480
thinking and say, "No, the other is wrong, and there's a better way to think about things." The same is true with Newton. The question I have is whether

109
00:20:24,480 --> 00:20:37,440
similar heuristics toward parsimony, aesthetics, and so on, would be equally useful across time and across disciplines, or whether you need different heuristics.

110
00:20:37,440 --> 00:20:46,160
The reason that's relevant is even if we can't build a verification loop for science, maybe if the taste tests point in the same direction, you can at least encode that bias

111
00:20:46,160 --> 00:21:01,360
